  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 254 AM MDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nFor Monday through Thursday, the upper-level trough swings \nthrough from the southwest that could potentially bring in a \ncold front Wednesday afternoon and Thursday morning. This \npattern should bring chances of showers into the area. with the \nchances of showers, it is unclear exactly where and when these \nshowers will be. However, the showers will likely be light over \nthe area. Temperatures are forecast to be in the 70s and then \n60s. There is some uncertainty with the timing of the cold front\nas it could either slow down or speed up. If the cold front \nslows down, we could expect showers to be later in Thursday with\nwarmer temperatures. However, if the cold front speeds up we \nwill have showers much earlier than expected with the majority \nof the showers happening on Wednesday and cooler temperatures.",
